While the older C-style method (`rand() % 20`) is common, it is strongly discouraged in modern C++ because it introduces "modulo bias," meaning some numbers will appear slightly more often than others.

Here is the standard, modern way to do it:

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <random>

